; ai.eval - where a monster can stand, and where a thing can come to rest
; (code-review batch 33: C58, C57, C74). tools\AITest.py runs this and JUDGES
; it; on its own it only reports. Every section header is `=== <name> ===` and
; the judge reads the readouts between one header and the next, so a section
; must stay self-contained.
;
; Everything runs in lockstep at timescale 0: nothing moves between lines, only
; inside a `step`, so a section's readouts describe exactly the time it stepped.
logecho on
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 11

; --- C58: a brazier's square is no side ----------------------------------------
; crypt1 as shipped. The brazier at 9,4 stands between the party at 8,4 and the
; skeleton at 10,4 and hides the party from it, so a bolt has to wake it. The
; brazier's square used to be handed out as the nearest side: no path reaches a
; brazier, and the skeleton stood still for as long as the party stayed put.
echo === brazier ===
goto crypt1
tp 8 4
face e
; Maren's Fire Bolt, learned and trained enough that it cannot fizzle.
learn 2 fire
learn 2 project
setskill 2 fire 5
monsters
tally reset
cast 2 0 fire project
step 5
monsters
tally

; --- C57: a kiter takes no side ------------------------------------------------
; A dead end has ONE side. The mage (a caster: it kites) stands nearer the party
; than the brute, so formation used to give it that side - which it never walks
; to - and the brute, finding it taken, held its own square for good. Both see
; the party down the corridor's axis from the room, so neither needs waking.
; Sampled every second: the mage must be seen KITING - its shots, `mshots=`,
; which only a kiter fires - while the brute is still on its way, or the brute's
; arrival would prove nothing (a mage that never stirred takes no side under any
; rule).
;   arena room 9 4: room 10..18 x 8..16, corridor 14,17..20, party at 14,20
echo === deadend ===
goto eval_arena
arena room 9 4
mapinfo
heal
face n
spawn skel_mage 14 15 south 1 up
spawn skel_warrior 14 13 south 1 up
tally reset
step 1
monsters
tally
step 1
monsters
tally
step 1
monsters
tally
step 1
monsters
tally
step 1
monsters
tally
step 1
monsters
tally
step 1
monsters
tally
step 1
monsters
tally
step 1
monsters
tally
step 1
monsters
tally

; --- C57: a body that takes no side still fills the one it stands on -----------
; A coward (it always flees) stands on the party's north side, dazzled so it
; cannot run. It takes no side, but it FILLS that one: the brute coming from the
; north, whose nearest side it is, must be sent round to another and swing from
; there. A side the coward stood on read as empty once kiters and fleers were
; left out of formation; the brute was sent to it, its last step was refused
; every time, and it stood two squares off for good.
;   arena room 9 4 again: the party at the room's centre, 14,12
echo === sidefill ===
arena room 9 4
heal
tp 14 12
face n
spawn skel_coward 14 11 south 1 up
effect dazzle ahead 1 30
spawn skel_warrior 14 8 south 1 up
tally reset
step 8
monsters
tally
heal

; --- C74: a pit is no floor to rest on -----------------------------------------
; A pit at 3,4 in crypt1's room, against its west wall (its other half, a
; ceiling hole, lands on crypt2 at 3,4 - in memory only, nothing is saved).
; A drop onto it is refused (a click there would throw instead); one beside it
; is laid. A throw that ends against the wall beyond it backs off along its
; flight to the first square a thing can rest on, and that is not the pit.
; The party WALKS onto 4,4 rather than `tp` there: a drop needs the square seen,
; and only a step reveals the squares round the party.
echo === pit-drop ===
reset
goto crypt1
stairadd pit 3 4
tp 6 4
face w
forward 2
step 2
pos
face w
expect-refuse drop rock 3 4
face e
drop rock 5 4
castsvc floor 3 4
castsvc floor 5 4

echo === pit-throw ===
tp 5 4
face w
tally reset
throw rock
step 3
castsvc floor 3 4
castsvc floor 4 4
tally

; A flask SHATTERS where its flight ends and leaves nothing to hang over a
; shaft: thrown west from 4,4 it stops in the wall at 2,4 and bursts over the
; pit at 3,4 - not pulled back onto the thrower's own square, as the rule for a
; thing that comes to REST would have it (`landat=` is where it came down).
echo === pit-flask ===
tp 4 4
face w
heal
tally reset
throw fire_flask
step 3
tally
heal

; The party can stand on a hole: the stairwell at 1,1 is where it arrives coming
; up from crypt2. A rock thrown north into the wall at 1,0 comes down on the
; party's own square - never past it, behind the thrower at 1,2.
echo === stair-throw ===
tp 1 1
face n
tally reset
throw rock
step 3
pos
castsvc floor 1 1
castsvc floor 1 2
tally

; The party at 3,5 has two open squares beside it, the pit to the north and
; 4,5 to the east. A skeleton at 3,3 used to take the pit - the nearer side -
; and fight from over the shaft. It must go round by 4,3 and 4,4 instead.
; Sampled every quarter second: a step takes it about half a second.
echo === pit-walk ===
tp 3 5
face n
spawn skel_warrior 3 3 south 1 up
tally reset
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
step 0.25
monsters
tally

; Nothing puts a monster on a pit, whatever moves it. The Gust shove plans no
; path: it steps a body square by square, refused by FreeSlotInCell alone - the
; same refusal that guards every monster that never uses the BFS (a kiter, a
; fleer). The BFS's own half (the snapshot's blocked grid) hides that one's
; absence on the walk above, so this asks it on its own: shoved three squares
; west from 5,4, a skeleton goes one and stops at 4,4, short of the pit at 3,4 -
; the wall at 2,4 would have stopped it ON the pit. No time passes: the shove
; commits its steps at once.
echo === pit-shove ===
tp 6 4
face w
spawn skel_bare 5 4 east 1 up
monsters
castsvc shove 3
monsters

echo === end ===
state
